s":45,"objectID":"50487185","points":273,"story_id":50487185,"title":"After 600 experiments, here's what I discovered about JEPA world models","updated_at":"2026-11-14T13:29:37Z","url":"https://haddyalchaer.com/jepa"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"maximilianburke"},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Monkey Island: all 13 versions side by side"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://monkeyisland.pages.dev/"}},"_tags":["story","author_maximilianburke","story_50493904","front_page"],"author":"maximilianburke","children":[50494840,50494901,50495031,50495110,50495149,50495174,50495332,50495403,50495416,50495469,50495474,50495482,50495511,50495555,50495592,50495649,50495651,50495766,50495785,50495836,50495850,50495856,50495906,50495920,50496080,50496182,50496261,50496272,50496280,50496304,50496333,50496335,50496348,50496380,50496640,50496673,50496689,50496793,50496916],"created_at":"2026-11-14T04:23:30Z","created_at_i":1794630210,"num_comments":80,"objectID":"50493904","points":250,"story_id":50493904,"title":"Monkey Island: all 13 versions side by side","updated_at":"2026-11-14T13:45:09Z","url":"https://monkeyisland.pages.dev/"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"simonebrunozzi"},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"FM-1 Workbench"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://open.m-vave.com/fm1-workbench"}},"_tags":["story","author_simonebrunozzi","story_50488325","front_page"],"author":"simonebrunozzi","children":[50488608,50488678,50488747,50488748,50488801,50488832,50488870,50489042,50489071,50489151,50489162,50489221,50489330,50489337,50489424,50489561,50489625,50490114,50490192,50490522,50490948,50491047,50491982,50492122,50492589,50493227,50496856],"created_at":"2026-11-13T19:14:02Z","created_at_i":1794597242,"num_comments":160,"objectID":"50488325","points":247,"story_id":50488325,"title":"FM-1 Workbench","updated_at":"2026-11-14T13:39:39Z","url":"https://open.m-vave.com/fm1-workbench"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"juscha1"},"story_text":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Technical Write-up: <a href=\"https://www.justinchavez.com/blog/isometric-sf-how/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.justinchavez.com/blog/isometric-sf-how/</a><p>Hi HN! Showcasing this fun project. I took 1300 square miles of the SF Bay Area from Google Photorealistic 3D Tiles and transformed them into a cohesive pixel map. It's really fun to explore and stumble upon various famous landmarks like Apple Park, Palace of Fine Arts, or UC Berkeley.<p>The technicals involve using Nano Banana 2 to train a Qwen-Image-Edit 2511 LoRA which is used to prototype the style and generation methods. For final map I used Qwen to train a Klein 4B LoRA which reproduced the style at 1/4 of the cost. More details in the blog post.<p>Let me know what you think! I really enjoyed this process of fine-tuning smaller open source models.<p>If I did the map with Nano Banana 2 it would have cost around 7k USD!<p>Credit for the idea goes to Isometric NYC."},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Show HN: Isometric SF \u2013 A pixel-art map of the SF Bay Area"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://isometricsf.com/"}},"_tags":["story","author_juscha1","story_50487228","show_hn","front_page"],"author":"juscha1","children":[50487635,50487714,50487747,50487765,50487783,50487812,50487887,50487941,50488197,50488534,50488784,50488981,50489051,50489116,50489153,50489230,50489341,50489691,50489708,50489743,50490242,50490413,50490455,50490456,50490486,50490489,50490773,50490874,50491325,50491861,50492394,50492480,50492511,50493575,50493779,50496703],"created_at":"2026-11-13T17:58:37Z","created_at_i":1794592717,"num_comments":73,"objectID":"50487228","points":226,"story_id":50487228,"story_text":"Technical Write-up: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.justinchavez.com&#x2F;blog&#x2F;isometric-sf-how&#x2F;\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.justinchavez.com&#x2F;blog&#x2F;isometric-sf-how&#x2F;</a><p>Hi HN! Showcasing this fun project. I took 1300 square miles of the SF Bay Area from Google Photorealistic 3D Tiles and transformed them into a cohesive pixel map. It&#x27;s really fun to explore and stumble upon various famous landmarks like Apple Park, Palace of Fine Arts, or UC Berkeley.<p>The technicals involve using Nano Banana 2 to train a Qwen-Image-Edit 2511 LoRA which is used to prototype the style and generation methods. For final map I used Qwen to train a Klein 4B LoRA which reproduced the style at 1&#x2F;4 of the cost. More details in the blog post.<p>Let me know what you think! I really enjoyed this process of fine-tuning smaller open source models.<p>If I did the map with Nano Banana 2 it would have cost around 7k USD!<p>Credit for the idea goes to Isometric NYC.","title":"Show HN: Isometric SF \u2013 A pixel-art map of the SF Bay Area","updated_at":"2026-11-14T13:29:09Z","url":"https://isometricsf.com/"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"cosmic_quanta"},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"A technical vision for the Haskell ecosystem"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://discourse.haskell.org/t/a-technical-vision-for-the-haskell-ecosystem/15078"}},"_tags":["story","author_cosmic_quanta","story_50484235","front_page"],"author":"cosmic_quanta","children":[50484978,50485183,50485264,50485513,50485715,50485788,50486026,50486169,50486405,50486428,50486664,50487028,50487363,50488427,50488851,50489876,50491974,50492881],"created_at":"2026-11-13T14:43:12Z","created_at_i":1794580992,"num_comments":136,"objectID":"50484235","points":221,"story_id":50484235,"title":"A technical vision for the Haskell ecosystem","updated_at":"2026-11-14T13:45:37Z","url":"https://discourse.haskell.org/t/a-technical-vi